      "worked": "The included angles follow from the differences between the bearings:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\angle AOB&=220^\\circ-100^\\circ=120^\\circ\\\\\\angle BOC&=310^\\circ-220^\\circ=90^\\circ\\\\\\angle COA&=360^\\circ-(310^\\circ-100^\\circ)=150^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\n\nApply the cosine rule to each side:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}AB&=\\sqrt{25^2+40^2-2(25)(40)\\cos120^\\circ}\\\\AB&=\\sqrt{3225}\\text{ m}\\\\BC&=\\sqrt{40^2+50^2-2(40)(50)\\cos90^\\circ}\\\\BC&=\\sqrt{4100}\\text{ m}\\\\CA&=\\sqrt{50^2+25^2-2(50)(25)\\cos150^\\circ}\\\\CA&=\\sqrt{3125+1250\\sqrt3}\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P&=\\sqrt{3225}+\\sqrt{4100}+\\sqrt{3125+1250\\sqrt3}\\\\P&\\approx193.5531486117\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe perimeter is 193.6 m, correct to one decimal place.",
